  "ingredients": [
    "1/2 cup cocoa nibs",
    "1 cup almond flour",
    "1/2 cup unsweetened shredded coconut",
    "1/3 cup erythritol",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt",
    "1/4 cup butter (melted)",
    "1/2 cup almond butter",
    "2 large egg",
    "25 drop liquid stevia",
    "1/4 cup heavy whipping cream",
    "10 drop liquid stevia",
    "1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1/8 teaspoon guar gum"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 350F. In a large mixing bowl, combine the cocoa nibs, almond flour, coconut flakes, erythritol, and salt.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-coconut-chip-cookies/#wprm-recipe-52273-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_3342.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt the butter in the microwave. Add the almond butter, eggs, and liquid stevia and stir to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-coconut-chip-cookies/#wprm-recipe-52273-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_3350.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slowly combine the dry ingredients with the wet ingredient mixture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-coconut-chip-cookies/#wprm-recipe-52273-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_3358.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spoon the cookie dough onto a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or a Silpat, ensuring that the cookies are evenly spaced.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-coconut-chip-cookies/#wprm-recipe-52273-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_3366.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Flatten the cookies with the back of a spoon.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-coconut-chip-cookies/#wprm-recipe-52273-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_3368.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake 20–25 minutes or until golden brown on the edges. Remove from the oven and place on a cooling rack to cool.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-coconut-chip-cookies/#wprm-recipe-52273-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_3372.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, create a glaze by combining the heavy cream, sweetener, and vanilla in a small mixer or immersion blender. Slowly add the guar gum while blending to thicken the glaze.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-coconut-chip-cookies/#wprm-recipe-52273-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_3375.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Glaze the top of the cookies. The mixture should be relatively thick, but it can be placed in the refrigerator briefly to thicken it up more.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-coconut-chip-cookies/#wprm-recipe-52273-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_3381.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-coconut-chip-cookies/#wprm-recipe-52273-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/LowCarbCoconutChipCookiesLong-Copy.jpg"
    }
  ],
